    "title": "German Teens Land in Oklahoma, Get Caught in I-35 Crash 20 Minutes Later - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Sousa ,\n11 hours ago Two German teenagers had been on American soil for only about 20 minutes when their ride from the airport ended up crumpled on the shoulder of Interstate 35 in Logan County, Oklahoma. Temperatures on the roadway reached 106 degrees as they waited, stranded, for help. That help arrived in the form of an Oklahoma Highway Patrol trooper who ended up doing far more than directing traffic. Read full article",
